## FSD Feature Architecture Map: MommaERP/Gidape

I've mapped the precise conventions for your React+Supabase ERP. Here's the scaffolding blueprint for the "ouvidoria" feature:

### 1. FEATURE STRUCTURE & BARREL EXPORT PATTERN

**Path:** `C:/Users/olive_/OneDrive/Documentos/codigo/Momma/momma-stock-insight/src/features/funcionarios/index.ts`

```typescript
/**
 * @module features/funcionarios — Core HR / DP/RH (completo)
 */

export { default as FuncionariosPage } from './ui/Funcionarios.page';
export { default as CargosPage } from './ui/Cargos.page';
export { default as NovoFuncionarioPage } from './ui/NovoFuncionario.page';
export { default as FuncionarioPerfilPage } from './ui/FuncionarioPerfil.page';
// ... other pages
export { AlertaExperienciaBanner } from './ui/AlertaExperienciaBanner';
export { EditarFuncionarioDialog } from './ui/EditarFuncionarioDialog';
```

**Convention:** Each feature has:
- **Barrel file** at `src/features/{feature}/index.ts` exporting all public components & pages
- **UI pages** named `*.page.tsx` (never just `.tsx`)
- **Model hooks** in `model/` directory (data fetching, business logic)
- **Lib utilities** in `lib/` (helpers, validation, storage, PDF generation)
- **Type definitions** in `types.ts` or co-located

**Directory structure:**
```
src/features/ouvidoria/
├── index.ts              # Barrel export
├── types.ts              # Type definitions
├── lib/
│   ├── permissions.ts    # Feature-specific permission helpers
│   ├── storage.ts        # Supabase access
│   └── validation.ts     # Form validation
├── model/
│   ├── useOuvidoriaList.ts
│   ├── useOuvidoriaDetail.ts
│   └── useOuvidoriaStats.ts
└── ui/
    ├── Ouvidoria.page.tsx        # Master list (owners only)
    ├── OuvidoriaDetail.page.tsx   # View complaint detail
    ├── OuvidoriaForm.page.tsx     # Anonymous submission form
    ├── components/
    │   ├── OuvidoriaCard.tsx
    │   └── StatusBadge.tsx
    └── dialogs/
        └── ResponderOuvidoriaDialog.tsx
```

For reference on real structure, see `src/features/encomendas/index.ts`:
